AiTask qa5_t12_same_weekday_swing {
  label: 'QA5 T12 Same-Weekday Revenue Swing'
  description: 'Alerts only when yesterday’s governed revenue moves more than 20% versus the same weekday one week earlier.'

  brief: @md
    Using @Dataset:ecommerce_official, run fresh queries in the workspace timezone. Define **yesterday** as the fully completed calendar date immediately before the task run date, and define **same weekday last week** as the calendar date exactly seven days before yesterday. Exclude the current partial calendar date.

    Calculate the dataset-defined `revenue` metric for each date, filtering by `orders.created_at` for each complete calendar-date window. Retain unrounded revenue values for every calculation. Only when same-weekday-last-week revenue is non-zero, calculate percentage change as `(yesterday revenue - same-weekday-last-week revenue) / same-weekday-last-week revenue` using the unrounded values. Present revenues as currency and identify both calendar dates.

    Use the available AI delivery capability only after evaluating these mutually exclusive conditions:
    - If percentage change is strictly less than -20%, send exactly one Slack post to **#nhity-test**. Its message must begin exactly with **[QA5 T12]** and include both dates, both revenues, and the percentage change. Also calculate revenue for both dates by `countries.name` and separately by `categories.name`. For each segment, calculate its unrounded absolute revenue delta as yesterday minus same-weekday-last-week revenue. Report concise top contributors to the decrease by ranking all negative country/category segment deltas from most negative upward, clearly labelling each as country or category. Do not imply that country and category contributions can be summed, and do not make causal claims.
    - If percentage change is strictly greater than 20%, send exactly one email to **nhi.ty@holistics.io**. Its subject must begin exactly with **[QA5 T12]**. The body must be a one-line note that includes both dates, both revenues, and the percentage increase.
    - If percentage change is from -20% through +20% inclusive, same-weekday-last-week revenue is zero, either comparison date has missing or non-comparable data, or the fresh query fails, send no email, Slack post, or other delivery.

    Never send both a Slack post and an email for one task run.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - Fresh queries against @Dataset:ecommerce_official use the dataset-defined `revenue` metric and workspace-timezone calendar-day windows based on `orders.created_at`: yesterday is the fully completed date immediately before the run and comparison date is exactly seven calendar days earlier; no current partial date is included.
    - The percentage change is calculated from unrounded overall revenue as `(yesterday - same-weekday-last-week) / same-weekday-last-week` only when prior revenue is non-zero.
    - A strictly less-than -20% change produces exactly one Slack post to #nhity-test and no email. The message begins exactly with [QA5 T12], includes both dates, both currency revenues, and percentage change, and lists concise country/category decrease contributors using `countries.name` and `categories.name`, ranked by negative unrounded absolute revenue delta with segment types clearly labelled.
    - A strictly greater-than 20% change produces exactly one email to nhi.ty@holistics.io and no Slack post. Its subject begins exactly with [QA5 T12], and its one-line body includes both dates, both revenues, and percentage increase.
    - Changes from -20% through +20% inclusive, zero/undefined prior revenue, missing or non-comparable data, and fresh-query failure produce no delivery of any kind.
    - The delivery branches are mutually exclusive, no branch sends duplicate deliveries, and all alerts are grounded in fresh data without unsupported causal claims.
  ;;
}